{title: 435 - The Glory Song}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #435 • (ALL PAUSES OBSERVED) • 9.10.9.10}
{lyricist: Charles H. Gabriel}
{composer: Charles H. Gabriel}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 435}
{meta: tune (ALL PAUSES OBSERVED)}
{meta: meter 9.10.9.10}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C/G]When all [G]my labors [F#dim]and [G]trails are o’er,
[G]And I am [C/G]safe [G]on [D7]that beautiful [G/D]shore,
[G]Just to be near the Lord I adore,
[F#dim]Will through the [Bm/F#]ages [D/A]be glory [G]for [C/G]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[G]O that [D/F#]will be
[Em]Glory [D/F#]for me, [Am]Glory [D/A]for me,
[A7]Glory [D/A]for me; [A7]When by [Am]His grace
[Am]I shall look on His face,
[D/A]That will [Em/B]be glory, [D/A]be [C/G]glory [G]for me.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C/G]When, by [G]the gift of [F#dim]His infinite [G]grace,
[G]I am accorded [D7]in heaven [G]a place,
[G]Just to be there and to look on His face,
[F#dim]Will through the [Bm/F#]ages [D/A]be glory [G]for [C/G]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C/G]Friends will [G]be there I [F#dim]have loved [G]long ago;
[G]Joy like a [C/G]river [D7]around [G/D]me will flow,
[G]Yet, just a smile form my Savior, I know,
[F#dim]Will through the [Bm/F#]ages [D/A]be glory [G]for [C/G]me.
{end_of_verse}
